<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<data-extraction-rules>
    <!--
      What is in this backup is a health log: body weight over time, what you ate, what
      you lifted. It should survive a reinstall (that is the point of backing it up) and
      it should not be readable by anyone but you.

      disableIfNoEncryptionCapabilities="true" is the control that makes both true at
      once. Android's cloud backup is end-to-end encrypted with the device's screen-lock
      secret, which Google does not hold — but only on a device that has a screen lock
      and the hardware to do it. This flag says: if that is not available, do not upload
      at all. A phone with no lock screen backs nothing up rather than shipping a
      readable copy of your weight history to a server.

      Device transfer is phone-to-phone over a local link and carries no such condition.
    -->
    <!--
      Progress photos are deliberately NOT in the cloud backup, and that is a
      decision rather than an oversight.

      The rest of this is numbers. Encrypted on a server with a key Google does not
      hold, a weight history is a reasonable trade for surviving a lost phone.
      Photographs of somebody's body are a different question, and it is not one to
      answer on their behalf by defaulting to upload. The cost is real and is stated
      on the photos screen: reinstalling loses them.

      Device transfer below does include them. That is a local link between two
      phones the person is holding, not a copy on someone else's computer.
    -->
    <cloud-backup disableIfNoEncryptionCapabilities="true">
        <include domain="database" path="gym.db" />
        <include domain="database" path="gym.db-wal" />
        <include domain="file" path="datastore/" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="photos/" />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <include domain="database" path="gym.db" />
        <include domain="database" path="gym.db-wal" />
        <include domain="file" path="datastore/" />
        <include domain="file" path="photos/" />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
